president Trump signing the largest  economic stimulus bill a relief bill in  US history as states across the country  ramp up efforts to battle the fast  spread of coronavirus scientists are  scrambling to develop a vaccine and  therapeutics as we speak joining me  right now is South Carolina Republican  Senator Lindsey Graham he's chairman of  the Senate Judiciary Committee mr.  chairman it's always pleasure to see you  thanks very much for being here and you  as well have been wrangling with the  idea of whether or not to open the  economy during this pandemic but you say  you've spoken with dr. Fauci this  weekend and you want to err on the side  of caution yeah so I told the doctor  pouchy and theirs we're at war with the  virus there's a spring campaign plan a  summer campaign plan and a fall campaign  plan this will come back in the fall but  I think the heat in the summer will  lower transmissions the virus generally  doesn't do well in heat so here's what  dr. pouchy said to reopen the economy  you have to have a breakthrough in  testing we got to get testing back in  real time not four or five days so if  you got a County out there with no  infections the only way we can safely  open that county up for business is to  have a testing regime we don't have  today so I would wait they got warmer  before I tried to open up any parts of  the economy we need a risk assessment  next week and before we actually start  turning the economy on I think we need a  breakthrough in testing and we need the  support from the summer that to me would  be the cautious approach well what about  the president saying look the cure  cannot be worse than the virus I mean we  are talking about a recession at hand  we're already in a contraction and we're  expecting the economy to worsen no  business no profits no economic activity  whatsoever yeah that's the balance we're  trying to make to try to create a bump  in the economy you don't want to create  create a spike in the disease the  president said safety first economic  rebounding second this package is going  to be a lifeline to people out of work  it's going to be a lifeline to  businesses who are who have no revenue  so this bill we passed is going to help  people for a couple of months the summer  will be here before you know it in the  spring  what I would do is ramp up my medical  supplies I try to focus on testing  antibiotics and therapies to destroy the  disease in the fall so this risk  assessment that's coming out next week  about what parts of the economy you may  reopen I don't think you can safely open  up any part of the economy until we have  more testing let me let me ask you about  this stimulus bill this relief package  if you will it's more of a relief  package than anything else you had issue  with the loophole around unemployment  basically giving money to people to stay  at home explain that for us senator okay  so if you make $15 an hour for a 40-hour  week that's 600 dollars a week my goal  was to make sure that in the  unemployment part of the package we made  you hold that you're laid off no fault  to your own you'd get $600 a week what  we did in the package is we plussed up  unemployment benefits so you'll get 926  dollars a week if you live in South  Carolina we increased your pay by 50%  that's going to make it harder to get  people back into the workforce it's  going to incentivize people not to go  back into the workforce and it's going  to make it harder for people to hire new  employees if you're Amazon and Walmart  the hourly wage not to work in South  Carolina is 23 dollars and 14 cents I'm  all for helping people how did this  happen they tell us at the state level  it would take six to eight months to  create a computer program to pay the  difference between the state  unemployment benefit in your actual age  so what do we do we just put six hundred  dollars on top of it so we took a $1,500  $15 an hour employee who was making six  hundred dollars working we're gonna pay  them nine hundred twenty six dollars in  South Carolina not to work we need to  fix that how are you gonna fix it get  some state to figure software that can  pay you the difference between the  maximum benefit per week of three twenty  six and six hundred dollars they tell me  that can't be done we sent two men to  the moon now Steven minuchin this is not  his fault we have a six hundred dollar  federal benefit on top of the state  benefit we have a situation where people  getting a hundred percent pay raise not  to work we have got to fix that some  smart person needs develop software that  can pay your actual wages not increase  your wages and unemployment well take  take us behind the curtain and to tell  us how this all shook out senator  because Nancy Pelosi said she did  jujitsu on this relief bill to get it  where it needs to be and this morning  this weekend she is saying that the  president is fiddling around while  people are dying senator know what she  said she's blaming the president the  United States for people dying because  of the way he's led the country that's  the most shameful disgusting statement  by any politician in modern history let  me tell you we've seen the best of  America from our citizens helping each  other  delivering groceries having special  shopping hours for sent senior citizens  she's the first politician to blame  another politician for people dying this  is the same Speaker of the House who  held up the bill in the Senate four days  because she wanted same-day voting she  wanted carbon neutrality for the  airlines she wanted 75 million dollars  for the Endowment for the Humanities and  25 million dollars for the Kennedy  Center she is the one that held up the  package in the Senate four days to get  the green New Deal put in a recovery  package so it's the most shameful  disgusting thing I've heard yet and it  needs to stop  well you you agree to send 25 million  dollars to the Kennedy Center you put  that in a so-called really oh because  she wouldn't let them yeah so she put a  gun to her head and said we will not get  this through the house until you put  twenty five million dollars with a  Kennedy Center she wanted the entire new  grid a new Green Deal in the package she  wanted to have every airline has to be  carbon neutral by 2025 what the hell's  that got to do with saving lives were  affected by the coronavirus she had the  entire green New Deal in the package we  took most of the garbage out but for her  to blame this president for causing loss  of life after she held up the relief  package four days to get a liberal  special-interest shopping list in the  bill is pretty disgusting it's  absolutely extraordinary senator it's  good to see this money thanks very much  for joining me

